<title>SINGAPORE: Thai Oil refinery runs flat out despite margins.</title>
<headline>Thai Oil refinery runs flat out despite margins.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiner Thai Oil Co Ltd is maintaining full runs at its 220,000 barrel-per-day refinery in spite of weak margins, a source close to the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The source said margins were very weak but the refinery did not have any cuts in thoughputs planned as yet.</p>
<p>The refinery located at Sri Racha on the eastern seaboard is 49 percent owned by the Petroleum Authority of Thailand with 15 percent held by Anglo-Dutch Shell, 4.75 percent by Caltex, the U.S. joint venture between Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp with the remaining 31.2 percent owned by private investors.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
